# Commit and Merge Requested Changes

- After implementing and verifying any user-requested repository change, commit it on a `codex/` feature branch.
- Fetch the latest remote default branch before merging.
- Push the feature branch, merge it into the current default branch, and push the merged default branch to GitHub.
- Confirm the remote default branch contains the merge commit and report the result.
- If GitHub integration triggers a deployment, verify its production status when deployment context is relevant.
- Skip this workflow only when the user explicitly requests local-only or uncommitted work.
